{minji} claims to be an "automated apparatus". Does that make it an
operatorless cabra ? I'd think so. I think that our natlang bias is making
us think that {minji} refers only to machines in a more traditional sense.

Also, I thought that {sarji} was more for a human sort of relationship of
support, somewhat like sidju. Maybe zbepi ? zbepi fi lo pruni, in
particular ?

.i mi'e la tsani mu'o

